"""Q19 round 2: rewrite the Q19 result as an interval of scenarios (idempotent patch on /output/report.json)."""
import json
p='/output/report.json'; d=json.load(open(p)); R=d['results']
q=[x for x in R if x['quantity'].startswith('Q19')][0]
q['value']=('HEADLINE (conditional, not a confirmation): the true HCN N/S T43/T32 is NOT established either way. Observed (Xb4f beam 5.72x3.54", s82) 1.262+-0.074 (HCO+ 1.164+-0.064); team-a p0022 raw ratio reproduced (1.257 Xb55 beam); their MCMC was NOT re-run. '
 'Q23 ramp: N/S x0.98+-0.025. Observed = true x D, D=(R47/R4f)_N/(R47/R4f)_S. D needed to reach unity: 1.24 (HCN), 1.14 (HCO+); independently bounded D from our Q12 relative-recovery priors is only <=1.034 (HCN), so unity is reached only with assumption-dependent scenarios. '
 'INTERVAL OF SCENARIOS, HCN N/S true (median [68%]): none (ramp only) 1.24 [1.16,1.32]; A, Q12 priors one-sided 1.22 [1.14,1.30] (2.5-3 sigma above 1); B, continuum anchor measured IN THE LINE BEAM (Xb47 and Xb4f continuum convolved to 5.72x3.54; aperture-matched; s101): continuum (47/4f)_N/(47/4f)_S = 1.15 (peak), 1.21 (point), 1.23 (r<1.5"), 1.17 (r<2.5") (mean 1.19, aperture sd 0.04; the 8.95x5.98" beam of the previous round gave 1.14/1.21/1.01/0.99 because that beam blends N and S 5.1" apart), anchor error taken 0.10 (>= aperture spread, registration, alpha) -> true N/S 1.00-1.07 depending on aperture, aperture mean 1.04 [0.92,1.17] (dalpha sd 0.3: 1.0-1.07 with 68% +-0.16); C, team-a physical uv model (not re-run) 0.97 [0.87,1.09]. '
 'Range of central values 0.97-1.24; scenarios A and B pooled WITHOUT C: wA=0.25/0.5/0.75 -> 1.10 [0.92,1.25] / 1.16 [0.97,1.27] (P>1 0.80) / 1.19 [1.06,1.29] (P>1 0.90): the pool is a weight judgement, not a likelihood combination, and the "<1 sigma, consistent with unity" statement of the previous round is withdrawn. '
 'BRIDGE CONTROL (HCN, same continuum anchor, s101): observed S/Bridge 0.99+-0.11, N/Bridge 1.25+-0.13. The anchor that removes N/S would make N/Bridge true 1.21 [1.05,1.39] and S/Bridge 1.14 [0.98,1.32] (P>1 0.8-0.9): i.e. it does not make the nuclei equal to the (extended) Bridge, it just moves the excess from N-over-S to both nuclei over the Bridge. If recovery depended simply on source extension, S and Bridge (both extended) would be filtered alike and the observed S~Bridge, N>both pattern would stand; if the continuum 47/4f ratio traces recovery, S/Bridge should be ~1.14 (1.4 sigma over the observed 0.99). The data cannot choose: the pattern is N-specific (N compact, steeper/different continuum alpha, or a real excitation difference) or an N,S,Bridge-dependent recovery. '
 'Xb4d (0.94x0.74") J3 smoothed to the Xb4f beam vs Xb4f J3 (s102): S(4f)/S(4d smoothed) HCN N 1.16, S 1.36, Bridge 1.17 (HCO+ 1.17, 1.30, 1.20): Xb4d loses 3-2 flux, S more than N or Bridge, so S is the more extended / more filtering-prone source (supports the sign of the one-sided prior) but this bounds Xb4d, not the Xb4f 3-2 or Xb47 4-3 recovery, so it does not bound D. '
 'Tbg / IR pumping: T43/T32 ratio of ratios is a data ratio, independent of Tbg; Tbg enters only the Tk conversion. Existing fits (s73/s74): Tbg 5 K S ladders Tk 20-80 K (dchi2(80)=3.1), N 65-150 K; Tbg 10 K S 20-30 K only, N 30-100 K, i.e. higher Tbg widens, not closes, an N-S Tk gap in that 8-datum fit; Tbg>5 K is not supported (beam-averaged dust Tbg,eff 3.0-3.7 K, Q16); pumping weakly constrained. N/S Tk ratio from the four ladders 1.3-1.6 [0.7-2.7], P(Tk_N>Tk_S)=0.6-0.67: not significant (team-a extended-gas T_N/T_S 1.2 [0.96,1.43]). '
 'WHAT WOULD DECIDE IT: visibility-level (matched uv-range) imaging of J=3 and J=4 on the common baseline range (>=~15-30 m, where Xb47 and Xb4f overlap) for N and S; or a measurement of Xb47/Xb4f recovery from a model of the extended emission using the visibilities, rather than image-plane priors.')
q['uncertainty']=('ratio of ratios: stat+registration 0.074 (HCN), 0.064 (HCO+); recovery D model-dependent: scenario central values 0.97-1.24; continuum anchor 0.10 (aperture sd 0.04, registration, alpha); pools depend on weights (HCN 1.10-1.19, 68% widths +-0.15); N/Bridge and S/Bridge +-0.11-0.13 stat')
q['confidence']='low'
for a in q['assumptions']:
    if a['name']=='beam': a['value']='Xb4f native 5.72x3.54 PA82 for lines AND for the continuum anchor (Xb47, Xb4f continuum convolved to it; peak, point, mean within r<1.5", 2.5"); the earlier 8.95x5.98" anchor (blended N+S) is superseded'
    if a['name']=='continuum anchor': a['value']='D_line = D_cont assumed (same filtering of line and continuum, equal continuum alpha for N and S; dalpha sd 0 and 0.3 tested); sig_c>=0.10; continuum may have its own alpha/size structure (free-free, compact dust), so this is an assumption, not a measured anchor; Bridge control shows it over-corrects S/Bridge by ~1.14'
    if a['name']=='pooling': a['value']='A+B pool shown for three weights, C excluded (not re-run); no likelihood combination'
q['evidence']='s100_q19_NS_recovery.py (out/q19/s100.txt), s101_q19_cont_anchor_bridge.py (out/q19/s101.txt: line-beam anchor, Bridge control, pool sensitivity), s102_q19_xb4d_vs_xb4f_32.py (out/q19/s102.txt), s103_update_report_q19r2.py; inputs out/q16b/s82.txt, out/q16/s74.txt, /snapshots/team-a-s09/out/q8c'
for x in R:
    if x['quantity'].startswith('Q16: matched-beam 4-3'):
        i=x['value'].find('[Q19 amendment')
        if i>=0: x['value']=x['value'][:i]+('[Q19 amendment: the HCN N/S 1.26 (2.9 sigma) is the UNCORRECTED ratio. With the Q23 ramp it is 1.24; with our Q12 recovery priors alone 1.22 [1.14,1.30]; with a line-beam continuum anchor 1.00-1.07; with the unreviewed team-a uv model 0.97. The true N/S is not established either way (scenario range 0.97-1.24); the continuum anchor over-corrects S/Bridge (1.14). See Q19.]')
for r in d['recipe']:
    if r['description'].startswith('Q19'):
        r['description']+='; round 2: line-beam continuum anchor, Bridge control, pool sensitivity (s101-s103)'
        for s in ('s101_q19_cont_anchor_bridge.py','s102_q19_xb4d_vs_xb4f_32.py','s103_update_report_q19r2.py'):
            if '/workspace/scripts/'+s not in r['scripts']: r['scripts'].append('/workspace/scripts/'+s)
i=d['interpretation'].find(' Q19:')
if i>=0:
    j=d['interpretation'].find('claimed.',i)+len('claimed.')
    d['interpretation']=d['interpretation'][:i]+' Q19: the N>S ladder contrast (HCN T43/T32 N/S 1.26 raw, 1.24 after ramp) is reproduced by team-a p0022 but its removal by differential Xb47/Xb4f recovery rests on assumptions: true N/S lies between 0.97 and 1.24 depending on the recovery scenario (our priors 1.22; line-beam continuum anchor 1.0-1.07; team-a model 0.97) and is not established either way; no N-S excitation difference is claimed, none is excluded.'+d['interpretation'][j:]
json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=1)
